    {
      "source_number": "733",
      "independent_solution": "Use t=(sqrt(t))^2 and cancel only nonzero factors: 2/sqrt(2)=sqrt(2), -5/sqrt(5)=-sqrt(5), 10/(3sqrt(10))=sqrt(10)/3, -a/(3sqrt(a))=-sqrt(a)/3. The last original fraction requires a>=0 for the radical and a!=0 for its denominator, hence a>0. The simplified formula's value at a=0 does not extend the original fraction's domain.",
